{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_336","type":"agent_message","text":"Done. Both files pass syntax checks and the leftovers are the intended hook-tracking variables.\n\n**Implemented**\n- `scripts/lib/paired-ablation.mjs` + `.d.mts`: pure aggregation — paired seeds, trial plan, activation check, p50/p95, tokens proxy, misblocks, safety violations, paired bootstrap 95% CI, Cohen's h, and a verdict function that reads only the pre-registered metric/budget. `pass^k` is delegated to E01's aggregator rather than reimplemented.\n- `scripts/paired-ablation-run.mjs`: drives the real `RuntimeMemoryStore` for both conditions.\n- `shared/agent-dev/paired-ablation-fixture.json`: 24 cases × 3 repetitions × 2 conditions, fixed insert order, identical access sequence, roles stratified by `memoryType` so the corpus can't pre-align with the treatment's per-type weights.\n- Two unit tests, harness task + rule specs, and `e02-paired-ablation.md` / `e02-acceptance.json` / `E02-SHA256SUMS`.\n\n**Result (honest)**\n- Activation proven: retained sets differ in 24/24 cases, 72/72 paired trials.\n- Success 0.125 → 0.625; `pass^k` 0.125 → 0.625; paired Δ **+0.50**, 95% CI **[0.25, 0.75]**; misblocks 66 → 27; tokens proxy 139.17 → 126.79. Verdict `benefit`, no budget breached.\n- I also added a null control (same policy both arms) which returns exactly zero effect, and a determinism check across runs — the effect is not an artifact.\n\n**Two things you should know**\n- Both arms silently evict `sensitivity: \"secret\"` facts without the compliance hook firing (baseline 69, treatment 9) — the FIFO trim path never calls it. This is a **pre-existing defect**, recorded as a residual and deliberately not fixed here. Verdict logic gates on *introduced* regression rather than letting a baseline defect mask the comparison.\n- `typecheck`, `scoped lint`, `harness run --dry-run`, and `check-duplicate-assets` could **not** run: `node_modules` is absent (installation prohibited) and the workspace has no `.git`, so the diff base can't resolve. They're recorded as not-run, never as passes. Tests ran via a local vitest-compatible shim, also disclosed in the acceptance file.\n\nPre-existing repo failures I left alone: `check-spec-lifecycle` flags E01 and O02 specs missing `lifecycleStatus`; `reliability-aggregation-boundary.md` lacks a `type` field. Fixing either would have broken their published hash manifests, so I restored E01's file byte-exactly (all 8 hashes verified)."}}
